ome of my  friends and i distributed flyers  condemning the iraqi invasion until we  were warned we might be killed if the  iraqi sauce  the iraqi sauce  reactors have destroyed everything in  kuwait  this they stripped the supermarkets of  food the pharmacies of medicine  the factories of medical surprise  supplies  ransacked their houses and tortured  neighbors and friends  i saw and talked to a friend of mine  after his torture and released by the  iraqis  he is 22 but he looked as though he  could have been an old man  the iraqis dunked his head into a  swimming pool until he almost drowned  they pulled out his fingernails and  applied electric shock to sensitive  private parts of his body  he was lucky to survive  if an iraqi soldier was found dead in a  neighborhood  they burned to the ground all the houses  in the general vicinity and would not  let firefighters come until  until the  only ash and rebel was left  the iraqis were making fun of president  bush and verbally and physically abusing  my family and me on our way out of  kuwait  we only did so because life in kuwait  became unbearable  they have forced us to hide bernard to  every everything identifying our country  and our government  i want to emphasize that kuwait is our  mother and then they are our father  we repeat  we repeated this on the roofs of our  houses in kuwait until the iraq is  beginning shooting at us  and we shall repeat it again  i'm glad i am 15 old enough to remember  kuwait before so damascus and destroyed  it and young enough to rebuild it thank  you mayor i thank you let me thank all  of our witnesses uh  we've uh  passed eight years  in the existence of the congressional  human rights caucus we've had scores of  hearings  about human rights abuses throughout the  world  and i know my co-chairman tom lantos  will join me  in telling you that we have never heard  in all this time  in all circumstances  a record of inhumanity and brutality  and sadism  as the ones that the witnesses have  given us  today  i don't know how  the  people of the  civilized countries of this world  can fail  to do everything within their power  to remove this  scourge  from the face of our earth  and the witnesses  by providing to us  eyewitness accounts  and reports  detailing  the conduct of the iraqi  soldiers  under the command of sudan hussein  have done a great service to their  country and to ours and to all countries  of the world  who must join together  and take whatever action may be  necessary  to free the people of kuwait  from this aggression and brutality  tom lentos  well let me first express my deepest  thanks to all of you  you have performed a  service of  incalculable value  and one can only hope and pray that  every american and indeed every citizen  of every civilized country  we'll hear your story  there are rare moments in history  when we are confronted with  human depravity of  incredible proportions  we had the killing fields in cambodia  we had the holocaust  with millions  innocent  killed  and now we have  the rape  of the people of kuwait  i do want to ask some questions  if you'll allow me  of  three members of the panel  ruth deborah and beth  because they represent to me  very fine  examples of young american women  were brought up in a free and open  and democratic society where human  rights are respected  and they were thrust into the nightmare  of  terrorist gang  engaging in actions  that we associate with  the dark moments of human history  so let me begin with you ruth if i may  where were you born  in memphis tennessee will you take a mic  and you went to elementary and high  school  in memphis  your brothers and sisters i have three  older sisters three older sisters  since you have come home  have you told them this story  yes sir what is their reaction  just it's so unbelieving for them to  realize that  that i lived through it they understand  what saddam hussein and his army are  capable of but it was  quite unbelievable for them to to  realize that their baby sister lived  through all of that and was able to get  out and tell the story  have you spoken to church groups or  other groups in in the community  yes sir i've been real active in memphis  with the world affairs council and  speaking to gifted children at several  schools and  i'm happy to do that  now ruth do people truly believe your  story not in the sense that they would  doubt your veracity but can they  comprehend  the enormity of the cruelty that you  were exposed to i think it's hard for  americans  we live so nice  in our country in america  to comprehend  the terrors  and the nightmares people suffered  i i can't answer that i know it's hard  to realize that people can do this to  other people  but the people in iraq  are capable of anything and everything  in the worst ways  and they've shown that to me  how they've treated the people in kuwait  and other foreigners there  best let me ask you this have you spoken  to to various groups in your community  where are you living now  i'm i live in monticello iowa with my  parents  and i have many people i when i first  came back i told people that i'd be  willing to come and speak to them about  my experiences and about what's  happening in kuwait  i've talked to various organizations  around eastern iowa  and also to socially conscious churches  and to many schools  may i come to you deborah  you um have  shaken up all of us  even those who have seen horror first  hand like myself  what has been your reception in in your  community where you live now when you  spoke of of your experiences  people have been reduced to tears they  just they can't  comprehend it i mean still  i've watched these things with my own  eyes and still i'm  sometimes i'm just just not convinced  that i really lived through all of that  that i made it and  every night i wake up in the middle of  the night i'm wondering are they doing  those things to my husband to his  families  you know so i've pretty well stayed away  from church and different things because  it's still hard for me myself to accept  but i got a very warm reception from the  people  i understand before we conclude i'd like  to call on my distinguished friend and  colleague from rhode island  thank you mr chairman  uh i too  greatly appreciate your strength and  your courage and and your willingness to  testify here today  too often  the world disbelieves  the atrocities that occur  they wish to live a fantasy to think  that the world is a very peaceful place  and that somehow these things never  occur  and it's only through  words and testimony that you've provided  here  that we can help to make people who are  idealistic realist  and that we can then create that realism  into some foreign policy which hopefully  can prevent  this  continued atrocity in the world  i certainly as a human being  find it difficult to understand how we  can continue to sit and just permit  the continued atrocities of someone who  has obviously forfeited the right to be  called a human being saddam hussein  he has permitted as the head of his  country  atrocities which none of us can  comprehend fully  because those of us who sit here have  not experienced the enormousness of the  horrors that go with those sort of  atrocities  perhaps  your testimony  will be the basis for this country  waking up to understanding that we are  not immune  just because  we are across the ocean  from this sort of human rights abuse  that our citizens  still remain in that country  that we have by some estimates 3 000  people  who this very moment may be  terrorized and tortured  by this very uh  inhuman  regime  and so you have done a service not just  to kuwait  but for all mankind because we must tell  the world  of the enormousness of what is going on  we appreciate and thank you very much  it was  51 years ago  that adolf hitler unleashed  unspeakable horrors on  mankind and the initial reaction of  vast numbers  was one of this belief  [Music]  or lack of interest  saddam hussein  has now unleashed on the people of  kuwait  unspeakable horrors  he is ready to unleash unspeakable  horrors  to other nations in the area  and it is the responsibility of all of  us  to awaken a  an indifferent  and disinterested  world community  to what this new hitler means  with your  presence and with your courageous and  moving testimony you have done mankind a  major service  the congressional human rights caucus if  it has done nothing in the last eight  years  but bring this one hearing  to the attention of the american people  it has served its purpose  i want to thank all of you this hearing  is concluded  [Music]  that concludes this hearing on alleged  human rights violations in kuwait for  further information you may contact the  congressional human rights caucus in  washington dc the zip code is 20515  coming up in just a moment live coverage  of the united states senate  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

